Request specifications let you define reusable request configurations. They're essential for DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) test code.

**What Are Request Specifications?**

Request specifications encapsulate common request configuration:

```java
// Without RequestSpecification (repetitive)
given()
    .baseUri("https://api.example.com")
    .header("Content-Type", "application/json")
    .header("Accept", "application/json")
    .auth().oauth2(token)
.when()
    .get("/users")
.then()
    ...;

// Same configuration repeated in every test
```

**Creating a Request Specification:**

```java
import io.restassured.builder.RequestSpecBuilder;
import io.restassured.specification.RequestSpecification;

public class Specs {

    public static RequestSpecification baseRequestSpec() {
        return new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .setBaseUri("https://api.example.com")
            .setBasePath("/v1")
            .setPort(443)
            .setContentType(ContentType.JSON)
            .setAccept(ContentType.JSON)
            .addHeader("X-API-Version", "2025-04-01")
            .addHeader("User-Agent", "REST-Assured-Tests")
            .addCookie("tracking", "abc123")
            .setRelaxedHTTPSValidation()  // For self-signed certs
            .setUrlEncodingEnabled(false)  // Disable automatic encoding
            .build();
    }

    public static RequestSpecification authenticatedRequestSpec(String token) {
        return new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .addRequestSpecification(baseRequestSpec())
            .setAuth(oauth2(token))
            .build();
    }

    public static RequestSpecification adminRequestSpec() {
        return new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .addRequestSpecification(authenticatedRequestSpec(getAdminToken()))
            .addHeader("X-Admin-Mode", "true")
            .build();
    }
}
```

**Using Request Specifications:**

```java
import static com.example.Specs.*;

public class UserTests {

    @Test
    public void testGetUsers() {
        given()
            .spec(baseRequestSpec())
        .when()
            .get("/users")
        .then()
            .statusCode(200);
    }

    @Test
    public void testCreateUserWithAuth() {
        String token = TokenManager.getToken();

        given()
            .spec(authenticatedRequestSpec(token))
            .body(UserPayloads.validUser())
        .when()
            .post("/users")
        .then()
            .statusCode(201);
    }

    @Test
    public void testAdminOnlyEndpoint() {
        given()
            .spec(adminRequestSpec())
        .when()
            .get("/admin/stats")
        .then()
            .statusCode(200);
    }
}
```

**Dynamic Specifications:**

```java
public class DynamicSpecs {

    public static RequestSpecification specForEnvironment(String env) {
        RequestSpecBuilder builder = new RequestSpecBuilder();

        switch(env) {
            case "dev":
                builder.setBaseUri("http://localhost:8080");
                builder.setRelaxedHTTPSValidation();
                builder.addHeader("X-Env", "development");
                break;
            case "staging":
                builder.setBaseUri("https://staging-api.example.com");
                builder.setAuth(oauth2(getStagingToken()));
                break;
            case "prod":
                builder.setBaseUri("https://api.example.com");
                builder.setAuth(oauth2(getProdToken()));
                builder.addHeader("X-Env", "production");
                break;
        }

        return builder.build();
    }

    public static RequestSpecification withQueryParams(Map<String, String> params) {
        return new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .addQueryParams(params)
            .build();
    }
}

// Usage
@Test
public void testInDifferentEnvironments() {
    // Test in dev
    given()
        .spec(specForEnvironment("dev"))
        .get("/health")
    .then()
        .statusCode(200);

    // Test in staging
    given()
        .spec(specForEnvironment("staging"))
        .get("/health")
    .then()
        .statusCode(200);
}
```

**Request Specification with Logging:**

```java
public class LoggingSpecs {

    public static RequestSpecification withDetailedLogging() {
        return new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .setBaseUri("https://api.example.com")
            .addFilter(new RequestLoggingFilter())      // Log request
            .addFilter(new ResponseLoggingFilter())     // Log response
            .addFilter(new ErrorLoggingFilter())        // Log only on error
            .build();
    }

    public static RequestSpecification withCustomLogging() {
        return new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .setBaseUri("https://api.example.com")
            .addFilter((req, res, ctx) -> {
                System.out.println("Request: " + req.getMethod() + " " + req.getPath());
                long start = System.currentTimeMillis();
                Response response = ctx.next(req, res);
                long duration = System.currentTimeMillis() - start;
                System.out.println("Response: " + response.getStatusCode() + " (" + duration + "ms)");
                return response;
            })
            .build();
    }
}
```

**Specification Inheritance:**

```java
// Base spec for all tests
public abstract class BaseApiTest {

    protected static RequestSpecification spec;

    @BeforeAll
    public static void setup() {
        spec = new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .setBaseUri(Config.getBaseUrl())
            .setContentType(ContentType.JSON)
            .addFilter(new ResponseLoggingFilter())
            .build();
    }

    protected RequestSpecification withAuth(String token) {
        return new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .addRequestSpecification(spec)
            .setAuth(oauth2(token))
            .build();
    }
}

// Test class extends base
public class UserTests extends BaseApiTest {

    @Test
    public void testPublicEndpoint() {
        given()
            .spec(spec)  // Base spec without auth
        .when()
            .get("/public/info")
        .then()
            .statusCode(200);
    }

    @Test
    public void testProtectedEndpoint() {
        given()
            .spec(withAuth("user-token"))
        .when()
            .get("/users/me")
        .then()
            .statusCode(200);
    }
}
```

**Best Practices:**

| Practice | Why | How |
|----------|-----|-----|
| **Define base spec** | Avoid repetition | One spec for common config |
| **Chain specifications** | Build complexity | `addRequestSpecification()` |
| **Environment-specific** | Run anywhere | Config-driven specs |
| **Immutable specs** | Safety | Create new rather than modify |
| **Static imports** | Readability | `import static Specs.*` |

**Key Insight:** Request specifications are your foundation for maintainable tests. Invest time in designing them well, and every test becomes simpler.

Response specifications let you define reusable validation rules. They ensure consistent checking across your test suite.

**What Are Response Specifications?**

Response specifications encapsulate common response validations:

```java
import io.restassured.builder.ResponseSpecBuilder;
import io.restassured.specification.ResponseSpecification;
import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.*;

public class ResponseSpecs {

    // Standard success response
    public static ResponseSpecification successResponse() {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectStatusCode(200)
            .expectContentType(ContentType.JSON)
            .expectResponseTime(lessThan(2000L))
            .expectHeader("Cache-Control", notNullValue())
            .build();
    }

    // Created response (POST)
    public static ResponseSpecification createdResponse() {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectStatusCode(201)
            .expectHeader("Location", containsString("/"))
            .expectBody("createdAt", notNullValue())
            .build();
    }

    // No content response (DELETE)
    public static ResponseSpecification noContentResponse() {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectStatusCode(204)
            .expectBody(emptyOrNullString())
            .build();
    }

    // Error responses
    public static ResponseSpecification badRequestResponse() {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectStatusCode(400)
            .expectBody("error", notNullValue())
            .expectBody("message", notNullValue())
            .build();
    }

    public static ResponseSpecification notFoundResponse() {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectStatusCode(404)
            .expectBody("error", equalTo("Not Found"))
            .build();
    }

    public static ResponseSpecification unauthorizedResponse() {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectStatusCode(401)
            .expectBody("message", containsString("unauthorized"))
            .build();
    }
}
```

**Using Response Specifications:**

```java
import static com.example.ResponseSpecs.*;

public class UserTests {

    @Test
    public void testGetUser() {
        given()
            .spec(baseRequestSpec())
        .when()
            .get("/users/123")
        .then()
            .spec(successResponse())  // Reusable validation
            .body("id", equalTo(123))
            .body("name", notNullValue());
    }

    @Test
    public void testCreateUser() {
        given()
            .spec(baseRequestSpec())
            .body(validUser())
        .when()
            .post("/users")
        .then()
            .spec(createdResponse())
            .body("id", notNullValue());
    }

    @Test
    public void testDeleteUser() {
        given()
            .spec(adminRequestSpec())
            .pathParam("id", 123)
        .when()
            .delete("/users/{id}")
        .then()
            .spec(noContentResponse());
    }

    @Test
    public void testUserNotFound() {
        given()
            .spec(baseRequestSpec())
        .when()
            .get("/users/999999")
        .then()
            .spec(notFoundResponse());
    }
}
```

**Dynamic Response Specifications:**

```java
public class DynamicResponseSpecs {

    // Spec that depends on response data
    public static ResponseSpecification responseWithId(int expectedId) {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectStatusCode(200)
            .expectBody("id", equalTo(expectedId))
            .build();
    }

    // Spec for paginated responses
    public static ResponseSpecification paginatedResponse(int expectedPage, int expectedTotal) {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectStatusCode(200)
            .expectBody("page", equalTo(expectedPage))
            .expectBody("total", equalTo(expectedTotal))
            .expectBody("data.size()", greaterThan(0))
            .build();
    }

    // Spec based on content type
    public static ResponseSpecification responseForType(ContentType contentType) {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectContentType(contentType)
            .build();
    }
}

// Usage
@Test
public void testGetSpecificUser() {
    int userId = 123;

    given()
        .spec(baseRequestSpec())
        .pathParam("id", userId)
    .when()
        .get("/users/{id}")
    .then()
        .spec(responseWithId(userId));
}

@Test
public void testPaginatedUsers() {
    given()
        .spec(baseRequestSpec())
        .queryParam("page", 2)
        .queryParam("limit", 20)
    .when()
        .get("/users")
    .then()
        .spec(paginatedResponse(2, 100));
}
```

**Combining Request and Response Specs:**

```java
public class CombinedSpecs {

    public static void verifyGetRequest(String path, int expectedId) {
        given()
            .spec(RequestSpecs.baseSpec())
        .when()
            .get(path)
        .then()
            .spec(ResponseSpecs.successResponse())
            .body("id", equalTo(expectedId));
    }

    public static <T> T createResource(T payload, Class<T> responseClass) {
        return given()
            .spec(RequestSpecs.baseSpec())
            .body(payload)
        .when()
            .post()
        .then()
            .spec(ResponseSpecs.createdResponse())
            .extract()
            .as(responseClass);
    }
}
```

**Specification Inheritance with Response Specs:**

```java
public abstract class BaseApiTest {

    protected static RequestSpecification requestSpec;
    protected static ResponseSpecification responseSpec;

    @BeforeAll
    public static void setup() {
        requestSpec = new RequestSpecBuilder()
            .setBaseUri(Config.getBaseUrl())
            .setContentType(ContentType.JSON)
            .build();

        responseSpec = new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectContentType(ContentType.JSON)
            .expectResponseTime(lessThan(3000L))
            .build();
    }

    protected ResponseSpecification successWithBody(String key, Object value) {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .addResponseSpecification(responseSpec)
            .expectStatusCode(200)
            .expectBody(key, equalTo(value))
            .build();
    }
}

public class UserTest extends BaseApiTest {

    @Test
    public void testGetUser() {
        given()
            .spec(requestSpec)
        .when()
            .get("/users/123")
        .then()
            .spec(successWithBody("id", 123))
            .body("name", notNullValue());
    }
}
```

**Validation with Response Specs:**

```java
public class ValidationSpecs {

    // Schema validation (using JSON schema validator)
    public static ResponseSpecification matchesSchema(String schemaPath) {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectBody(matchesJsonSchemaInClasspath(schemaPath))
            .build();
    }

    // Business rule validation
    public static ResponseSpecification validUserResponse() {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectBody("email", matchesPattern("^[^@]+@[^@]+\\.[^@]+$"))
            .expectBody("age", allOf(greaterThanOrEqualTo(18), lessThan(150)))
            .build();
    }

    // Array validation
    public static ResponseSpecification nonEmptyArray(String path) {
        return new ResponseSpecBuilder()
            .expectBody(path + ".size()", greaterThan(0))
            .build();
    }
}
```

**Best Practices:**

| Practice | Why | How |
|----------|-----|-----|
| **Granular specs** | Reusability | Small, focused specifications |
| **Compose specs** | Flexibility | `addResponseSpecification()` |
| **Named specs** | Clarity | Method names describe purpose |
| **Default spec** | Consistency | Base spec for all tests |
| **Override when needed** | Precision | Test-specific overrides |

**Key Insight:** Response specifications encode your API contract into reusable assertions. They ensure every test validates the same baseline quality.

REST Assured provides built-in support for various authentication mechanisms. Here's how to handle them all.

**Authentication Types:**

```java
public class AuthenticationExamples {

    // 1. Basic Authentication
    @Test
    public void basicAuth() {
        given()
            .auth().basic("username", "password")
            .get("/secured")
        .then()
            .statusCode(200);
    }

    // 2. Digest Authentication
    @Test
    public void digestAuth() {
        given()
            .auth().digest("username", "password")
            .get("/secured")
        .then()
            .statusCode(200);
    }

    // 3. OAuth 2.0 (Bearer Token)
    @Test
    public void oauth2() {
        given()
            .auth().oauth2("your-access-token")
            .get("/secured")
        .then()
            .statusCode(200);
    }

    // 4. OAuth 1.0
    @Test
    public void oauth1() {
        given()
            .auth().oauth(
