Beyond basic stubbing, WireMock offers powerful features for complex testing scenarios. Master these to handle sophisticated mocking requirements.

**Priority-Based Stubbing**

When multiple stubs match, priority determines which one is used:

```java
// High priority - specific case
stubFor(get(urlEqualTo("/users/1"))
    .atPriority(1)  // Lower number = higher priority
    .willReturn(okJson("{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"John\"}")));

// Medium priority - all users except special cases
stubFor(get(urlPathMatching("/users/\\d+"))
    .atPriority(2)
    .willReturn(okJson("{\"name\":\"Regular User\"}")));

// Low priority - fallback for any user request
stubFor(get(urlPathStartingWith("/users"))
    .atPriority(3)
    .willReturn(okJson("{\"name\":\"Default\"}")));
```

**Custom Request Matchers**

```java
// Custom matcher using Java
stubFor(requestMatching("custom-matcher", (request) -> {
    String auth = request.getHeader("Authorization");
    String body = request.getBodyAsString();

    return auth != null && 
           auth.startsWith("Bearer ") && 
           body.contains("admin");
})).willReturn(ok());

// Matcher with parameters
stubFor(requestMatching(new RequestMatcherExtension() {
    @Override
    public MatchResult match(Request request, Parameters parameters) {
        String requiredRole = parameters.getString("role");
        String userRole = extractRoleFromToken(request.getHeader("Authorization"));

        return MatchResult.of(userRole.equals(requiredRole));
    }
}).withParameters(Parameters.one("role", "admin"))
    .willReturn(ok()));
```

**Webhook Notifications**

```java
// Trigger webhook when stub is matched
stubFor(post("/order")
    .willReturn(ok())
    .withPostServeAction("webhook", 
        webhook()
            .withMethod(POST)
            .withUrl("http://notification-service.com/order-created")
            .withHeader("Content-Type", "application/json")
            .withBody("{\"orderId\":\"{{jsonPath request.body '$.id'}}\"}")
            .withFixedDelay(100)));
```

**JWT Token Validation**

```java
// Custom matcher for JWT
stubFor(any(urlPathMatching("/secure/.*"))
    .andMatching((request) -> {
        String auth = request.getHeader("Authorization");
        if (auth == null || !auth.startsWith("Bearer ")) {
            return false;
        }

        String token = auth.substring(7);
        try {
            // Parse and validate JWT (simplified example)
            String[] parts = token.split("\\.");
            if (parts.length != 3) return false;

            String payload = new String(Base64.getDecoder().decode(parts[1]));
            return payload.contains("\"role\":\"admin\"");
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return false;
        }
    })
    .willReturn(ok()));
```

