**Pattern 6: Dependency Mirroring**

Create a complete mirror of all downstream dependencies:

```java
// Mirror multiple services
public class DependencyMirror {

    private final WireMockServer mockServer;
    private final Map<String, String> services;

    public DependencyMirror(int port, Map<String, String> services) {
        this.mockServer = new WireMockServer(options().port(port));
        this.services = services;
    }

    public void start() {
        mockServer.start();

        // Proxy all unknown requests
        mockServer.stubFor(any(anyUrl())
            .willReturn(aResponse()
                .proxiedFrom(services.get("default"))));

        // Specific service mappings
        for (Map.Entry<String, String> service : services.entrySet()) {
            if (service.getKey().equals("default")) continue;

            mockServer.stubFor(requestMatching(new ServiceMatcher(service.getKey()))
                .willReturn(aResponse()
                    .proxiedFrom(service.getValue())));
        }
    }

    private class ServiceMatcher extends RequestMatcherExtension {
        private final String servicePath;

        ServiceMatcher(String servicePath) {
            this.servicePath = servicePath;
        }

        @Override
        public MatchResult match(Request request, Parameters parameters) {
            return MatchResult.of(request.getUrl().startsWith(servicePath));
        }
    }
}
```

**Pattern 7: Data-Driven Virtual Services**

Drive mock responses from external data sources:

```java
// Mock backed by database or CSV
public class DataDrivenMock {

    private final List<Map<String, Object>> testData;

    public DataDrivenMock(String dataFile) {
        // Load test data from CSV, JSON, etc.
        this.testData = loadTestData(dataFile);
    }

    public void configureStubs() {
        for (int i = 0; i < testData.size(); i++) {
